# Peka — Co-op 2D Platform Puzzler

> Game Design Document (living draft). Filled out as we ideate.
>
> **Decided:** symmetric players + co-op verbs · local couch · mysterious/eerie tone

---

## 1. Description

A **2D co-op platform game** built around **cooperative puzzles**. Two players
progress through **one long level** together. The level is designed so it is
**impossible to complete solo** — every major obstacle requires both players to
act in coordination. The fun comes from communication, timing, and each player
controlling something the other depends on.

Tone is **mysterious and eerie** — sparse, atmospheric, story told through the
environment rather than text (Limbo / Inside lineage). The pair are small and
vulnerable; the world is large and unexplained.

**Core pillars**
- **Forced cooperation** — no section clears without two players.
- **Puzzle-first platforming** — movement is the verb; the brain-teaser is the challenge.
- **One handcrafted level** — a single, long, escalating journey rather than many short stages.
- **Wordless atmosphere** — eerie mood, environmental storytelling, minimal UI.

---

## 2. Cooperation Model — ✅ Symmetric + co-op verbs

Both players control **identical** characters with the **same abilities**. The
dependency comes from **obstacles that need two bodies** and **co-op verbs**,
not from asymmetric powers. Either player can be picked up by either person —
no "main character."

**Why this fits:** local couch + eerie tone + forced cooperation. Two identical
small figures in a hostile world reads cleanly in silhouette and keeps the
mechanics learnable for both players instantly.

### Cooperative verbs (the teamwork vocabulary) — _draft, to refine_
- **Hold-to-open** — one stands on a plate/lever to hold a gate while the other passes.
- **Boost** — one crouches/cups hands to launch the other to a higher ledge.
- **Catch / pull-up** — one hangs from a ledge, the other climbs over and pulls them up.
- **Counterweight** — both needed on a see-saw, pulley, or balance platform.
- **Carry** — one picks up and carries/throws the other across a gap.
- **Block & path** — one body holds a mechanism while the other's path opens.

- [ ] Lock the final list of ~4–6 verbs the whole level is built from
- [ ] Decide which verbs are "taught early" vs "combined late"

